<p>NOTE: The company said Q2 1996 net loss includes a write-off of $1,751,600 for patent costs and a $425,300 charge from a severance agreement with a former officer.  Excluding these charges, the net loss for current quarter decreased $450,200, or 21.1 percent compared to the same period last year.</p>
<p>The company said six months 1996 includes a write-off of patent costs and a severance charge (discussed above), which were partially offset by a $309,800 gain from the sale of T Cell Diagnostics Inc in March 1996.  Excluding these items for the 1996 period, net loss for the current six months decreased $676,000 or 15.7 percent compared to the first six months of 1996.</p>
<p>Full name is T Cell Sciences Inc.</p>
